## §1–§2 — Observe / Plan (per item, summarized; full per-item records in artifact dirs / this run dir)
- T233 (completion, queue #104): build sha 0cac34f4… stands from Wave 37 (16,832 B), segment 8.000 s. Cures priced in scores.md: (1) executable CONFIG-derived companions for every fixed census probe, at least CP4 companion moving under pressDurMs timing swap; (2) full-predicate enforcement — P7 grid-at-rest, P11 post-swap diff EMPTY with all instants filed, C probes labeled ==P3/P4/P7 execute full predicate sets or drop labels; (3) census completion — config-census §2 entries for seamStrokePx + cushionStrokePx reconciled mechanically; (4) fit vertical edge — tool-label baseline −102 px accounting, visibility interval measured or label re-anchored. Completion form: apply ONLY the filed cures → fresh own-checks + A6 legs → A13 receipt index re-reconciled (assertion inheritance whole) → ONE jev-prewave completion re-fire → on FIRE-WAVE, five-lens wave bound to that build; on HOLD, NO VERDICT, next re-fire PENDING AUTHORIZATION.
- T238 (first attempt, queue #105): Packet #13 (PES "Fresh Guacamole") @ 75–81 s — identity collapse: pestle mash. Mechanics (style-library techniques-endings.md §T238, read firsthand): pestle works bowl in repeated strokes; discrete objects (dice, cubes, houses, green flesh) progressively lose identities and merge into uniform green paste flecked with their colours; stop-motion increments — each stroke, fewer readable objects. Evidence: ev/t078-pestle-mash.jpg · clips/pestle-mash.mp4 in digest 2026-11-17-yt-dnjdjiwcfy. Consumer: DLC assembler ending containers. Variables: object set/counts, stroke count/durations, collapse fractions per stroke, paste colour/fleck colours, bowl/pestle geometry, palette, scale. Schedule basis to be named in per-item Plan (A7).
- T241 (first attempt, queue #106): Packet #14 (@ensan.besham "Hope = Failure (?)") @ 0–13 s — probability board as opening shot. Mechanics (techniques-openings.md §T241): opens mid-diagram — targeting-reticle icon at top, star figure inside magnifier circle, 40-icon population array below, conditional-probability line P(F|H) ≈ 0.98 with Bayes expansion typeset underneath; elements draw on in layers over first seconds — build order is the claim. Evidence: ev/001-bayes-board.jpg · ev/005-board-build-mid.jpg · clips/000-bayes-board-build.mp4 in digest 2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3. Consumer: DLC assembler opening / diagram containers. Variables: array count, formula text, layer order/timings, palette, icon geometry, scale.
- T242 (first attempt, queue #107): Packet #14 @ ≈6–18 s — the 2% bar chart. Mechanics (techniques-diagrams.md §T242): four tall empty bar outlines rise to a 100% axis; a tiny filled stub labelled 2% appears at base of first bar while star figure stands at right at full height; height ratio felt before statistic understood — growth order is the claim. Evidence: ev/010-two-percent-bars.jpg in same digest. Consumer: DLC assembler diagram containers. Variables: bar count/heights, stub percent/label, rise timings/order, figure height, palette.
- T243 (first attempt, queue #108): Packet #14 @ ≈13–27 s — calendar-of-days panel with crossed-out dates. Mechanics (techniques-diagrams.md §T243): rounded panel holds grid of day numerals; most struck through with diagonal slashes, two ringed, dashed drop-lines connect two crossed dates to a timeline below whose labels are also struck out; second panel with empty checkboxes joins it. Draw-on order: grid → strikes → drop-lines → timeline labels — named order is the claim. Evidence: ev/020-calendar-days.jpg · ev/026-calendar-tasks-crossout.jpg. Consumer: DLC assembler diagram / transition containers. Variables: grid size/day numerals, struck/ringed sets, drop-line targets, timeline labels, draw-on timings, palette.

