| F-2500/F-3500/F-4500 | census-2500/3500/4500.jpg | 2500/3500/4500 | 77.5/78.5/79.5 | 245772e5…86f8 / c26841ea…e39 / 6fdf1862…b9e | Fine frames extracted (sha in artifact census listing); intermediate stroke positions consistent with the 1 s states. |

**Motion findings:** motion instants — shot cut to close-up between 1000–1500 ms · pestle strokes: down at ≈2000 · raised at 3000/4000/5000 · down at ≈5500/6000 — a ≈840–1000 ms stroke cycle (down-phase + lift) carried in stop-motion increments (the source is stop-motion throughout: positions jump between frames, no smooth blur). Holds — the wide setup 0–≈1250 ms is a HOLD on the full set; no other true holds: every close-up census instant differs from its predecessor (count down, coverage up). What changes between states: readable count falls monotonically · green coverage rises monotonically · pestle alternates down (centre) / raised (right) · green slabs lose their boundaries (distinct at 1500 → merged by 4000 → invisible as slabs by 5000).
**Sub-beats:** SB-A wide setup hold (full set, pestle at rest) · SB-B close-up entry (pestle raised, set maximal) · SB-C..G strokes 1–5, each collapsing its assigned object cohort · SB-H final paste state (flecks only).
**Fine stroke census (jev-observe-exit charge 1, applied — 250 ms frames `census/fine-*.jpg`, viewed firsthand):** close-up already established at 1250 ms (fine-1250, sha 2289ee1e…) · CONTACT (pestle down, pressing right-of-centre) at 1750 ms (fine-1750, b26e1620…) · down-centre at 2000 ms · RAISED at 2750 ms (fine-2750, ae802931…) · CONTACT down-centre at 3750 ms (fine-3750, fd1b5934…) · CONTACT down-centre at 4750 ms (fine-4750, ed327a50…) with the paste already near-uniform on the left · down at 5500/6000 ms. Binding reading: ≈5 press cycles across 1500–6000 ms at ≈840–1000 ms per cycle. (AMENDED under codex-plan-review: the allocation is 5 × 900 ms with press peaks at 1900/2800/3700/4600/5500 ms — within 150 ms of a sampled contact at 1750–2000/3750/4750/5500; the earlier 840 ms fit's 4398 ms peak stood 352 ms from the nearest contact and was rejected on its face by the review.) **Hold reconciliation (AMENDED under codex-plan-review + jev-plan-exit):** §1.3's "no other true holds" stands for the SOURCE — the window ends mid-mash at 81.0 s with no source-observed terminal hold; the build carries NO end hold either (holdMs 0, completion AT 6000 ms = CP6); the settled final frame the ending container needs is supplied by the comparison's clamp holding the completed state, not by a build hold. One schedule stands: setup 1500 · 5 × 900 strokes · complete 6000 · duration 6000. Readable/fleck definitions (consistent throughout): readable = object still identifiable by kind at census size; fleck = a colour fragment no longer identifiable by kind.

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · bowlCx 320 · bowlCy 208 · bowlRx 218 · bowlRy 104 · bowlWallPx 14 · pasteInsetF 0.92 · pestleRx 64 · pestleRy 42 · pestleRestDx 196 · pestleRestDy -64 · pestleDipPx 34 · pestleLiftPx 26 · pestleHandleLenPx 74 · pestleHandleRxPx 17 · pestleSweepPx 118 · stepMs 100 · pressSteps 4 · pressLossShare 0.7 · readableThresh 0.5 · pasteStart 0.34 · fleckPx 7 · sinkPx 10 · deformShrink 0.55 · deformRound 0.9 · rngSeed 238 · labelFontPx 30 · toolLabelFontPx 28 · inputLabelDy 128 · toolLabelDy -146 · outputLabelDy 128 · fontFamily "Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif" · inputLabel "DICE · HOUSES · CUBES" · toolLabel "PESTLE MASH" · outputLabel "GUACAMOLE" · tSetupMs 0 · setupDurMs 1500 · strokeCount 5 · strokeDurMs 900 · holdMs 0 · easeStroke "easeInOut" · easeSetup "linear" · palette {board #8a6844, boardDark #6f5233, bowl #4a4a48, bowlDark #33322f, paste #79c142, pasteDark #5da334, die #d8262c, dieEdge #8f1218, pip #ffffff, house #159a8c, houseRoof #0d6e64, minidie #f2f2f2, minipip #222222, cube #17b3a6, pestle #55534e, pestleDark #3c3a36, labelInk #ffffff, labelHalo #3a2a18}`. (Schedule AMENDED under codex-plan-review: strokeDurMs 900 fitted to the fine-census contacts — press peaks at 1900/2800/3700/4600/5500 ms, within 150 ms of a sampled contact at 1750–2000/3750/4750/5500; holdMs 0 — completion lands AT the window edge 6000 ms = CP6, no designed hold; pressFrac is replaced by the step-exact pressSteps/stepsPerStroke pair.)
Array: `objects[24]` — `{kind, x, y, s, rot, pips, cs}`: x/y in bowl radii (−1..1), s = size px, cs = collapse stroke 0–4. Kind counts DERIVED: die 8 · house 6 · minidie 6 · cube 4 = 24. Cohort counts DERIVED from cs: 5 · 5 · 5 · 5 · 4 = 24 (count assertion: source cohort sum 24 = built objects.length 24, harness-printed).
Coefficients bound as keys (jev-plan-exit cure): `marksCutF 0.35 · slabBaseScale 0.55 · slabGrowScale 0.75 · labelSwitchF 0.5` — marks opacity = clamp((integrity − marksCutF)/(1 − marksCutF)) · slabScale = slabBaseScale + slabGrowScale×pasteP · label switch at collapsedFraction vs labelSwitchF. `easeStroke` application site: stateAt eases the RAW press curve (pressRaw → pressE) and the pestle's inter-stroke x travel; both raw and eased values are returned and receipted separately.
Object defaults (jev-plan-exit cure — the full allocation, 24 rows; kind counts die 8 · house 6 · minidie 6 · cube 4; cohort counts cs0–cs4 = 5·5·5·5·4. **Count disposition:** 24 is the BUILD allocation — the source census estimates ≈28 readable at CP1 and ≈30 at CP1500; the reduction is deliberate (fewer, larger objects keep kinds readable at phone size) and is printed here, never passed off as the source count):
`objects[24]` = die(-0.55,-0.30,34,-12,5,0) · die(0.10,-0.45,36,8,4,0) · house(-0.15,-0.05,30,0,0,0) · minidie(0.45,-0.20,18,20,3,0) · cube(-0.70,0.25,26,-8,0,0) · die(0.62,0.30,33,14,3,1) · house(0.30,0.05,29,-6,0,1) · minidie(-0.35,0.42,17,-18,5,1) · die(-0.05,0.28,35,5,6,1) · cube(0.05,-0.70,25,10,0,1) · house(-0.62,-0.62,28,12,0,2) · die(0.48,-0.58,32,-16,2,2) · minidie(0.72,-0.02,18,7,4,2) · cube(-0.28,-0.48,24,-4,0,2) · die(-0.48,0.58,31,18,4,2) · house(0.18,0.52,30,-10,0,3) · die(0.68,0.58,34,-7,5,3) · minidie(-0.08,-0.22,17,24,2,3) · cube(0.38,0.68,26,3,0,3) · house(-0.72,-0.05,30,9,0,3) · house(0.55,-0.38,27,16,0,4) · minidie(-0.18,0.68,18,-22,6,4) · die(0.02,0.02,33,-3,4,4) · minidie(0.80,0.38,16,11,3,4) — tuple = (kind, x, y, s, rot, pips, cs); pips applies to die/minidie (house/cube carry 0).
Array: `slabs[3]` — `{x, y, rx, ry}` (the three avocado-half slabs of §1.1 priced reading (2), bowl-relative): (-0.52,0.05,0.52,0.78) · (0.05,-0.28,0.55,0.72) · (0.55,0.12,0.50,0.80). Slab scale and union opacity derive from pasteP (below); slab boundary visibility = 1 − pasteP.
Derived (named, never stored): setupEnd=tSetupMs+setupDurMs (=1500) · stepsPerStroke=strokeDurMs/stepMs (=9, validated integer) · pressFrac=pressSteps/stepsPerStroke (=4/9) · strokeStart(k)=setupEnd+k×strokeDurMs (1500/2400/3300/4200/5100) · pressPeak(k)=strokeStart(k)+pressSteps×stepMs (1900/2800/3700/4600/5500) · mashEnd=setupEnd+strokeCount×strokeDurMs (=6000) · completeAtMs=mashEnd (=6000) · durationMs=mashEnd+holdMs (=6000) · **clock (codex-plan-review cure):** the active stroke is derived from RAW t by half-open intervals [strokeStart(k), strokeStart(k+1)) BEFORE quantization; inside the mash the evaluated instant is q = setupEnd + floor((t−setupEnd)/stepMs)×stepMs (q(1500)=1500 exactly; the setup act uses raw t and is NOT quantized — the source wide shot is live-action, named in §2.5) · **press-bound collapse (cure):** per-object loss during its stroke = pressLossShare × (step/pressSteps) for step ≤ pressSteps, then pressLossShare + (1−pressLossShare) × (step−pressSteps)/(stepsPerStroke−pressSteps) — 70% of identity loss rides the press descent, the rest the lift/grind; integrity = 1 − loss (before its stroke 1; after 0 → object renders as a fleck of its own colour) · **kind-marks bound to the same transition (cure):** pip/roof opacity = clamp((integrity − marksCutF)/(1 − marksCutF)) — the marks that make a kind readable die BEFORE the shape finishes blending, so modeled readability (integrity > readableThresh) never claims marks the state no longer shows · pasteP = pasteStart + (1−pasteStart) × collapsedFraction where collapsedFraction = Σ(1−integrity)/objects.length (denominator DERIVED from the validated nonempty array, never a literal) · readableCount = #{integrity > readableThresh} · fleckCount = #{integrity = 0} · slabScale = 0.55 + 0.75×pasteP · unionOpacity = pasteP · pestle state: setup → rest position (pestleRestDx/Dy), lifting in the setup's second half by pestleLiftPx to the raised pose; during stroke k → target x = bowlCx − pestleSweepPx + 2×pestleSweepPx×sweepFrac(k), sweepFrac = strokeCount>1 ? k/(strokeCount−1) : 0.5 (the strokeCount=1 case handled, cure), y dips by pestleDipPx × pressCurve(step) where pressCurve = step/pressSteps (step ≤ pressSteps) then (stepsPerStroke−step)/(stepsPerStroke−pressSteps); handle = rounded rect of pestleHandleLenPx × 2×pestleHandleRxPx above the head; at/after mashEnd → rests down-centre (the CP6 pose). **Validation:** setupDurMs/strokeDurMs/stepMs > 0, holdMs ≥ 0 (the zero hold is the selected schedule, jev-plan-exit cure); strokeDurMs divisible by stepMs; pressSteps in [1, stepsPerStroke); strokeCount positive integer; pressLossShare in (0,1); readableThresh in (0,1); pasteStart in [0,1); objects nonempty; every cs in [0, strokeCount); object |x|,|y| ≤ 0.92; a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; board rect; bowl group (outer wall ellipse + inner paste field); paste layer (codex-plan-review cure — the slab model): the 3 CONFIG slab ellipses (paste fill) scaled by slabScale with their boundaries visible early + a unifying paste ellipse whose opacity = unionOpacity, so slab boundaries are LOST as pasteP → 1 exactly as the census shows (distinct slabs at 1500 → merged by 4000 → invisible by 5000) + pasteDark texture blobs (seeded, positions derived from object index); objects layer — per object a group (die: rounded rect + pip circles · house: rect + roof polygon · minidie: small rect + dark pips · cube: rect) transformed by integrity (scale toward deformShrink floor then fleck, corner radius toward deformRound, fill blended toward paste, y sunk by sinkPx × (1−integrity), kind-marks — pips/roofs — fading on the marks curve, which reaches 0 at integrity 0.35, before the shape finishes blending); pestle group (ellipse head + handle rect) positioned by the stroke machine, drawn ABOVE the objects (real occlusion at stroke bottoms); three CONFIG label texts with EXCLUSIVE ownership (cure): input label opacity = 1 while collapsedFraction < 0.5 else 0, output label opacity = the complement — exactly one owns the stage at any instant (the A5 phase-exclusivity analogue; the harness asserts never both > 0); tool label rides above the bowl at toolLabelDy. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the per-stroke identity loss, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Hands — not built; the pestle moves by its own stroke machine (fleet diagram form for performed-action techniques, T233 precedent). (2) The wide→close-up shot cut (1000–1500 ms) is compressed onto the single stage: the build's setup act shows the same bowl at stage scale throughout (no zoom); the census cut is a camera change, not a state change — the STATE at 1500 (full set, pestle raised) is what the build binds. (3) The prior technique's chess pieces (CP0/CP1 left foreground) — set dressing of T14, omitted. (4) Texture realism of the stone bowl/paste — flat CONFIG colours + seeded dark blobs stand in for photographic texture; the technique priced is the collapse law, not the material render.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **segment-anchored** — build instant = census seg-rel ms exactly (offset 0). Departure table: CP0/CP1's wide-shot framing + chess dressing have no build counterpart (deferrals §2.2 (2)(3)); their BOUND STATE (readable = all 24, pasteP = pasteStart, pestle at rest) is the build's setup state.
Assertions (CONFIG expression → evaluated instant; receipts print raw phase + eased separately, full predicates over ALL objects; all expected values derived from the AMENDED clock: stepsPerStroke 9, pressSteps 4, pressLossShare 0.7):
- P0 setup start: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSetupMs)` → 0 ms: readable 24, flecks 0, pasteP = pasteStart (0.34), pestle at rest offset, input label owns stage (output opacity 0).
- P1 setup mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSetupMs + CONFIG.setupDurMs/2)` → 750 ms: readable 24, strokeIdx −1 (no stroke yet).
- P2 mash start (CP1500 anchor): `stateAt(CONFIG, setupEnd)` → 1500 ms: q = 1500 exactly, readable 24, pestle raised (liftP = 1), strokeIdx 0, step 0.
- P3 stroke-0 press mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, setupEnd + 2×CONFIG.stepMs)` → 1700 ms: step 2, loss = 0.7×2/4 = 0.35, cs-0 integrity 0.65 (raw), marks opacity = (0.65−0.35)/0.65 ≈ 0.4615, readable 24.
- P4 stroke-0 press peak: `stateAt(CONFIG, setupEnd + CONFIG.pressSteps×CONFIG.stepMs)` → 1900 ms: step 4, pressCurve = 1 (dip maximal), cs-0 loss 0.7, integrity 0.3, readable 19.
- C@2000 (CP2): `stateAt(CONFIG, 2000)` → strokeIdx 0, step 5, phase 5/9 ≈ 0.5556, loss = 0.7+0.3×1/5 = 0.76, cs-0 integrity 0.24, readable 19 (census ≈20).
- C@3000 (CP3): strokeIdx 1, step 6, loss = 0.7+0.3×2/5 = 0.82, readable 14 (census ≈18 — the §2.5 tension, printed beside, never fudged).
- C@4000 (CP4): strokeIdx 2, step 7, loss = 0.7+0.3×3/5 = 0.88, readable 9 (census ≈10).
- C@5000 (CP5): strokeIdx 3, step 8, loss = 0.7+0.3×4/5 = 0.94, readable 4 (census ≈6).
- C@5500 (F-5500): strokeIdx 4, step 4 (= press peak of stroke 4), loss 0.7, readable 0, flecks 20 (census: flecks only ✓).
- P5 complete = CP6 anchor: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)` → 6000 ms: readable 0, flecks 24, pasteP 1, unionOpacity 1, slab boundaries 0, output label owns stage. **Departure printed:** the specimen at 81.0 s still shows ≈1 partially readable red die at the top edge (it would fall to a stroke beyond the window); the build completes the collapse AT the window edge — guards cmd 8's zero-state probe binds the BUILD's prescribed end state, and the departure is named here, not hidden.
- P6 post-complete identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 150)` fully equal to P5 state — RAW FULL-STATE equality over the whole state object (the comparison clamp holds this state; it is not a source hold). durationMs = 6000.
- P7 quantization: `stateAt(CONFIG, 2001)` equals `stateAt(CONFIG, 2000)` on every mash-derived field (same stepMs bucket, q = 2000) AND `stateAt(CONFIG, 2100)` has step 6 ≠ step 5 — the stop-motion increment is executable, not asserted.
- P8 label exclusivity: at every probed instant, inputOpacity × outputOpacity = 0 and inputOpacity + outputOpacity = 1 (exactly one label owns the stage).
- Zero-state anchor (guards cmd 8): the END state is the zero-identity anchor — at P5, readableCount = 0 evaluated from the CONFIG expression `Σ (integrity > readableThresh)` printed raw, not a bare constant.
- **Extended fixed census probes (jev-plan-exit cure — every named checkpoint gets a fixed probe + its CONFIG-derived companion + full predicates):** C@0 (CP0) = P0 · C@1000 (CP1) → `stateAt(CONFIG, 1000)`: setup, readable 24, strokeIdx −1, pestle liftP = 1000/1500 eased printed · C@1250 (fine-1250, close-up established) → `stateAt(CONFIG, 1250)`: setup act, readable 24 (the build's single stage has no camera cut — the probe binds the STATE, §2.2 deferral (2)) · C@1750 (fine-1750 CONTACT) → companion P3/P4 form: `stateAt(CONFIG, 1750)`: strokeIdx 0, step 2, pressE printed · C@2750 (fine-2750 RAISED) → `stateAt(CONFIG, 2750)`: strokeIdx 1, step 3, pressRaw 0.75 — **POSE DEPARTURE priced below** · C@3750 (fine-3750 CONTACT) → `stateAt(CONFIG, 3750)`: strokeIdx 2, step 4, pressRaw 1.0 ✓ contact matches peak · C@4750 (fine-4750 CONTACT) → `stateAt(CONFIG, 4750)`: strokeIdx 3, step 5, pressRaw 0.8 · C@5750 (fine-5750) → `stateAt(CONFIG, 5750)`: strokeIdx 4, step 6, pressRaw 0.6, readable 0.
- **Pose-departure table (jev-plan-exit charge 1, priced alternative):** the allocation's stroke boundaries are FITTED, not observed; sampled source poses vs build poses: 1750 CONTACT vs build step-2 half-press (departure: build's first contact peaks 150 ms later at 1900) · 2000 DOWN vs build step-5 pressRaw 0.8 falling (small) · 2750 RAISED vs build step-3 pressRaw 0.75 (**the standing departure**: the build's stroke-1 peak at 2800 sits between the sampled lift at 2750 and the sampled contact at 3750 — no sampled contact binds it; it is the fitted midpoint of the 2400–3300 stroke) · 3000/4000/5000 RAISED vs build lift phases (pressRaw 0.4/0.29/0.14 falling — direction agrees) · 3750 CONTACT vs build peak 1.0 ✓ · 4750 CONTACT vs build 0.8 (near) · 5500/6000 DOWN vs build peak 1.0 at 5500 ✓ / complete-rest at 6000 ✓. The timing lens prices the schedule WITH this table on the record; no tolerance claim beyond it is made.

